            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura2/recipes-ventura2/plat-svc/files/99-valve-dac-init.rules",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "What is this numbering referring to?  I guess it is \"bus 3 or 6\" and \"address 0c, 0e, or 0f\"?  Can you comment that accordingly.  I think it would be clearer to separate bus 3 and 6 into separate udev rules, plus then we can delete bus 6 when EVT is no longer supported."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-ventura2/recipes-ventura2/plat-svc/files/99-valve-dac-init.rules",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eldin Lee",
                        "email": "eldin.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "eldin-lee"
                    },
                    "message": "I've separated the PVT and EVT rules and added comments to make the bus and address mapping clearer.\n\nHere is some additional information for the review:\n\n```bash\nroot@bmc:~# journalctl -u valve-dac-init@*\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc systemd[1]: Starting Valve DAC output voltage init (3-000c)...\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc systemd[1]: Starting Valve DAC output voltage init (3-000e)...\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc systemd[1]: Starting Valve DAC output voltage init (3-000f)...\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[542]: [3-000c] volt=10 raw=1013\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[542]: [3-000c] DAC set request sent\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[542]: [3-000c] DAC init success\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc systemd[1]: Starting Valve DAC output voltage init (6-000c)...\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc systemd[1]: Starting Valve DAC output voltage init (6-000e)...\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[548]: [3-000e] volt=10 raw=1013\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[548]: [3-000e] DAC set request sent\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[548]: [3-000e] DAC init success\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[554]: [3-000f] volt=10 raw=1013\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[554]: [3-000f] DAC set request sent\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[554]: [3-000f] DAC init success\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc systemd[1]: Starting Valve DAC output voltage init (6-000f)...\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[561]: [6-000c] I2C device not responding\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[566]: [6-000e] I2C device not responding\nMar 09 20:17:23 bmc valve-dac-init[571]: [6-000f] I2C device not responding\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: Finished Valve DAC output voltage init (3-000c).\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: Finished Valve DAC output voltage init (3-000e).\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: Finished Valve DAC output voltage init (3-000f).\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: valve-dac-init@6-000c.service: Main process exited, code=exited, status=1/FAILURE\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: :5:185m:5:185mvalve-dac-init@6-000c.service: Failed with result 'exit-code'.\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: Failed to start Valve DAC output voltage init (6-000c).\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: valve-dac-init@6-000e.service: Main process exited, code=exited, status=1/FAILURE\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: :5:185m:5:185mvalve-dac-init@6-000e.service: Failed with result 'exit-code'.\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: Failed to start Valve DAC output voltage init (6-000e).\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: valve-dac-init@6-000f.service: Main process exited, code=exited, status=1/FAILURE\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: :5:185m:5:185mvalve-dac-init@6-000f.service: Failed with result 'exit-code'.\nMar 09 20:17:25 bmc systemd[1]: Failed to start Valve DAC output voltage init (6-000f).\n```"
                }
            ],
